// The appearance cache: what the game's finished picture showed of a material, against what our model gives there, in
// two levels of cell of one table (AC_N cells of 16 uints, 8 probed):
// - by texture: per material, layer and place on its texture (at most 64 cells a side, read bilinear; a flat material
//   one cell). How the game shows each part of a texture, wherever it is, our diffuse colour Lt telling the light: the
//   patterns, glow and tints its other textures (masks we do not read) give, on what moves too, and where the screen
//   never showed that place.
// - by place: cells of 12 cm within 8 m of the camera, doubling with each doubling of the distance, per material and
//   facing (the normal's main axis: the two sides of a thin wall apart), read trilinear. What the game showed there
//   against what the texture level then gave (P): the light our model has not (its shadows' depth, occlusion, local
//   lights), over the texture's detail.
// Mode 13 claims a record's two cells and sets P, rt_late.comp sums the finished colour F (its reflections in), P
// and Lt into them, mode 14 halves the sums past 64 samples (about two seconds) and frees cells not seen for 30 s.
// A hit takes the texture cells' mean F', each channel varied as our colour here against our mean there (ac_col), else
// our fit's colour; times the place cells' F' over P.
